---
import Journey from '../../layouts/Journey.astro';
import Step from '../../components/journey/Step.astro';
import Next from '../../components/journey/Next.astro';
import More from '../../components/journey/More.astro';
import CopyPrompt from '../../components/site/CopyPrompt.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/nav';
---
<Journey chapter="check" first="done" title="Make it prove it" description="An agent reports done whether or not the work is right. A check between the agent and you sends wrong work back.">
  <Step id="done" title="It says “done” either way">
    <p>Six made-up jobs through <a href={url('journey/loop/')}>the loop from step 2</a>. Three come out wrong, drawn in orange, and all six reach you as “done”.</p>
  </Step>
  <Step id="tests" title="Put a check in the way">
    <p>A check now stands between the agent and you. A job that fails the tests goes back to the agent, not on to you.</p>
    <More title="A prompt for this">
      <CopyPrompt compact title="Ask for proof with the work">{`Before you tell me it is done:
1. Run the tests and paste the last lines of the output.
2. If the change shows on screen, open the page at phone width, take a screenshot and say what you see.
3. List what you could not check.`}</CopyPrompt>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="more" title="Each check sees one kind of wrong">
    <p>Three checks stand between the agent and you now. Switch one off and watch which job gets past.</p>
    <div class="pick" data-multi role="group" aria-label="Checks that are switched on">
      <button type="button" data-do="toggle" data-val="tests" data-default aria-pressed="true">Tests</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="toggle" data-val="look" data-default aria-pressed="true">A screenshot</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="toggle" data-val="review" data-default aria-pressed="true">A second model</button>
    </div>
    <More title="What each check is">
      <dl class="j-defs">
        <dt>Tests</dt><dd>A command the agent runs. It passes or it fails.</dd>
        <dt>A screenshot</dt><dd>The agent opens the page in a browser and looks at it.</dd>
        <dt>A second model</dt><dd>Another model reads the change without having seen how it was made.</dd>
      </dl>
    </More>
    <Next from="check" more={[{ href: 'explain/verification/', text: 'Checking the work' }]} />
  </Step>
</Journey>
